        "content": "<p>Hello everyone!</p>\n<p>I am excited to announce that our tactic <code>reap</code>, a neural tactic for general purpose step-prove is now public available, and is really easy for anyone to use.  With joint effort with <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110087\">@Kim Morrison</span> and PKU AI4Math group at Joint MATRIX / MFO Workshop, now there is no need for model deployment and no specified Lean version is required. <a href=\"https://github.com/frenzymath/reap\">Github repo</a>.</p>\n<p>We encourage everyone to try and welcome any feedback!</p>\n<h3>Quick start</h3>\n<p>If you are using <code>lakefile.lean</code> in your project, add the following line to the file.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">require</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"reap\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://github.com/frenzymath/reap.git\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"main\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Or if you are using <code>lakefile.toml</code>, add</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"TOML\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">[[require]]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"reap\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://github.com/frenzymath/reap.git\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">rev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"main\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>After that, <code>import Reap</code> in the file you are working on, then <code>reap</code>/<code>reap?</code> immediately works for you!</p>\n<h3>Mathlib built-in</h3>\n<p>Alternatively, we are working on a mathlib branch with <code>reap</code> built in, adding <code>reap</code> tactic into <code>Mathlib.Tactic.Common</code>. That will be very nice since you can then obtain <code>reap?</code> suggestions with absolutely no dependency required. </p>\n<p><code>reap</code> is designed to be simple and compatible to upstream, and could be easily merged into master at any proper time.</p>\n<p>To try our pr in sync with <code>master</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fetch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">https</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"n\">github</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">com</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">frenzymath</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">mathlib4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reap</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">reap</span>\n<span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">checkout</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reap</span>\n<span class=\"n\">lake</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cache</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--repo=frenzymath/mathlib4 get</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Build cache of this branch works at chance and may need a rebuild, and we are working to resolve this.</p>\n<h3>Highlights of <code>reap</code> tactic</h3>\n<p>In the Joint MATRIX / MFO Workshop at Melbourne, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110087\">@Kim Morrison</span>  and I tried few things in Mathlib and found it impressive.</p>\n<p>One of the first places we tried it out was in <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Topology/Algebra/ConstMulAction.html#set_smul_closure_subset\">docs#set_smul_closure_subset</a>. This lemma was chosen because it was added <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/29859\">by Yury few days before</a>, so there is no possibility <code>reap?</code> has seen it before (training cutoff was <code>v4.16.0</code>, but will be updating soon).</p>\n<p>Currently this theorem reads as</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set_smul_closure_subset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">closure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">closure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iUnion_smul_set</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iUnion₂_subset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">smul_closure_subset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">closure_mono</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">subset_biUnion_of_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hc</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>We started using <code>reap?</code> after the <code>simp only</code> call, finding the following steps:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set_smul_closure_subset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">closure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">closure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iUnion_smul_set</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- `reap?` suggestions start here:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">iUnion₂_subset_iff</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">smul_closure_subset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- This step didn't go through until we used `set_option tacticgenerator.num_samples 200`</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">closure_mono</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- At this point we diverge from the line Yury took, but it's still reasonable:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">subset_def</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mem_iUnion₂</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exists_prop</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- and finished!</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hy</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hy</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>We are really curious about how much more <code>reap</code> can make to simplify proof-writing. And we definitely need more feedback from community to help us improve this engine, front-end, better model, better retrieval, etc.</p>",
        "id": 542200044,
        "sender_full_name": "Yutong Wang",
        "timestamp": 1759216908
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Link to discussion thread <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"113488\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Reap.20tactic.20related/with/541142864\">#general &gt; Reap tactic related</a>. Please let us know how you feel about <code>reap</code> if you've tried in your project. Also for previous post <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113486-announce/topic/Reap.21.3A.20Yet.20another.20tactic.20for.20theorem-proving/near/536354349\">#announce &gt; Reap!: Yet another tactic for theorem-proving @ 💬</a>  for more info about <code>reap</code> itself.</p>",
